                <pb facs="0578" n="480" xml:id="pg480"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic">September 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 835.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 725, of the 28th ultimo, relative to the loss of the French
                    torpedo-boat destroyer <hi rendition="#italic">Framée</hi>, and to inform you in
                    reply that the Department approves your course in expressing the sympathy of
                    your embassy to the French Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
